COMMAND NAME: mppactivatemaster.sh

Reactivates the original primary master host and puts the currently 
active backup master host in standby mode again.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mppactivatemaster.sh -m <primary_master_host> [-a] [-q] [-l <logfile_directory>]

mppactivatemaster.sh [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mppactivatemaster.sh script will reactivate your original 
primary master instance that was previously taken out of operation. 
Use this script when you have activated a standby master host using 
mppactivatestandby.sh and now want to reinstate the original master 
host as the active master for the system. 

This script is run from the currently active backup master host, not 
the original primary master host you are activating. This script assumes 
that the data directories on both master hosts are in the same location, 
and that your Bizgres MPP system is currently operational using the 
backup master host.

The script will perform the following steps:

* Shutdown your Bizgres MPP system

* Copy the data directory from the backup master host to the primary 
  master host you are activating

* Update the MPP system catalog tables

* Initialize the backup master host as the standby again

* Restart the Bizgres MPP system with the primary master host

*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-m <primary_master_host>

Required. The host name of the original primary master 
host that you want to reactivate.

-a

Do not prompt the user for confirmation.

-q

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the 
screen, but is still written to the log file.

-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.

-?

Displays the online help.

-v

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and checksum of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Reactivate your original primary master host from the active 
backup master host:

mppactivatemaster.sh -m host08


